// Session config for every ROS 2 node that lives in the central island
// (navigation_manager_node, easynav_collaboration_mission_node, the
// fleet-wide rviz2, and any future tui/cli tool): connects to
// zenoh_router_central.json5. Shared by all of them -- no fixed "id" here
// (unlike the per-robot session configs), since the central router has no
// ACL that needs to recognize individual local clients by zid, so there's
// no reason to risk an id collision between simultaneously running
// central-side processes (see zenoh.md's prototype notes on why a shared
// fixed id broke a second concurrent session).
//
// mode: "peer" -- see robot_1/zenoh_session.json5 for why: "client" mode
// silently breaks delivery of TRANSIENT_LOCAL/latched publications (here,
// most importantly, the JSON payload published once on `/capabilities`) to
// a subscriber that joins after the one-shot publish, which is exactly
// mission_control's discovery pattern. (No `gossip.autoconnect` override
// here either -- see that file for why: it breaks the very delivery this
// mode change fixes.)
{
  mode: "peer",
  connect: { endpoints: ["tcp/127.0.0.1:7447"] },
  scouting: { multicast: { enabled: false } },
}
